en.question:
A road checks your average speed. Average speed = distance ÷ time.
The road is 10 km long. The slowest speed is 60 km/h. The fastest speed is 80 km/h.
Slower than 60: pay $3000;
1~20 km/h too fast: pay $4000;
21~40 km/h too fast: pay $5000;
more than 40 km/h too fast: pay $6000;

Input the driving time (minutes). Output the money to pay.
